Title: 0005-autobudget-service-spending
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0004-savefile-check-fclose.patch
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-17
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: Engine automatic budget settlement; all native and WASM targets

Problem:
  Automatic budget debits selected funding but records full service spending, giving full service effects after cuts.
Solution:
  Record allocated fireValue/policeValue/roadValue and update service effects after annual settlement, never during menu previews.
Validation:
  Host ASan/UBSan: tests/budget/run-tests.sh verifies real annual settlement
  reduces service effects without a test-side updateFundEffects() call.
  The native ABIv11 budget test also passes on AROS One.
Removal:
  Permanent engine correction; remove when the pinned upstream includes it.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/budget.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/budget.cpp
index aaaa0cf..2432fdd 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/budget.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/budget.cpp
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@ void Micropolis::initFundingLevel()
 void Micropolis::doBudget()
 {
     doBudgetNow(false);
+    // A yearly settlement changes paid service levels. Menu previews must not.
+    updateFundEffects();
 }
 
 
@@ -303,9 +305,10 @@ noMoney:
             Quad moreDough = (Quad)(taxFund - total);
             spend(-moreDough);
 
-            fireSpend = fireFund;
-            policeSpend = policeFund;
-            roadSpend = roadFund;
+            // Service effects must match the amounts actually funded above.
+            fireSpend = fireValue;
+            policeSpend = policeValue;
+            roadSpend = roadValue;
 
             mustDrawBudget = 1;
             doUpdateHeads();
